WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.260 --> 00:00:05.380
Daenerys Targaryen is known by many titles,
and on the latest episode of Game of Thrones,

00:00:05.380 --> 00:00:09.600
she gained another one, a name she insisted
she would never take on, as long as she could

00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:10.600
help it.

00:00:10.720 --> 00:00:13.760
Here's how the twist went down and what it
all means.

00:00:14.060 --> 00:00:19.320
Daenerys admits she has only known fear in
Westeros, not the love that her nephew, boyfriend,

00:00:19.320 --> 00:00:23.420
and potentially rival claimant to the Iron
Throne Jon Snow has come to receive.

00:00:23.680 --> 00:00:28.820
This realization, combined with her newfound
knowledge that her Master of Whisperers Varys

00:00:28.820 --> 00:00:33.010
committed treason against her in shifting
his loyalty to Jon, plus the recent death

00:00:33.010 --> 00:00:37.420
of her trusted adviser Missandei, pushes Daenerys
past her breaking point.

00:00:37.420 --> 00:00:42.260
The Mother of Dragons dives head-first into
the madness that her father, the so-called

00:00:42.260 --> 00:00:46.200
"Mad King," suffered when he sat on the Iron
Throne amidst Robert's Rebellion.

00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:51.500
In Episode 5, Dany became "The Mad Queen,"
destroying King's Landing and killing thousands

00:00:51.500 --> 00:00:56.200
of innocent men, women, and children on her
mission to unseat Cersei Lannister and take

00:00:56.200 --> 00:00:57.610
the Iron Throne herself.

00:00:57.900 --> 00:00:59.660
"The Iron Throne.

00:01:01.180 --> 00:01:03.820
Perhaps you should try wanting something else."

00:01:03.860 --> 00:01:08.200
Dany time and again has stated that she's
not a carbon copy of her father, and she wouldn't

00:01:08.200 --> 00:01:09.850
make the same mistakes he did.

00:01:10.280 --> 00:01:13.180
"I am not here to be Queen of the Ashes."

00:01:14.520 --> 00:01:19.200
But that's exactly what wound up happening
during this latest episode, in a moment many

00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:21.240
viewers felt was a wild twist.

00:01:21.240 --> 00:01:27.100
However, in the eyes of Game of Thrones showrunners,
Daenerys going mad wasn't exactly a big shock.

00:01:27.100 --> 00:01:31.960
David Benioff and Dan Weiss explained during
the show's "Inside the Episode" featurette

00:01:31.969 --> 00:01:36.450
that Thrones had long foreshadowed Dany's
spiraling into instability, and that there

00:01:36.450 --> 00:01:40.609
are plenty of clues sprinkled throughout past
seasons that signaled this dark turn would

00:01:40.609 --> 00:01:41.860
happen eventually.

00:01:41.860 --> 00:01:46.540
One such clue is the death of Daenerys' brother,
Viserys, back in Season 1.

00:01:46.540 --> 00:01:51.800
Dany didn't second-guess her decision to have
Khal Drogo pour molten gold over Viserys'

00:01:51.800 --> 00:01:55.880
head and refused to look away when the deed
was carried out, wanting to watch him suffer

00:01:55.880 --> 00:01:57.100
through the pain.

00:01:57.300 --> 00:01:59.720
"He was no dragon.

00:02:01.160 --> 00:02:03.580
Fire cannot kill a dragon."

00:02:03.980 --> 00:02:08.780
Daenerys has a history of killing, or ordering
others to kill on her behalf, and exhibiting

00:02:08.780 --> 00:02:11.260
no signs of hesitancy or remorse.

00:02:11.260 --> 00:02:15.791
She burnt a witch alive and almost relished
in her cries; she sentenced people to die

00:02:15.791 --> 00:02:17.890
in a vault and didn't think twice.

00:02:17.890 --> 00:02:22.080
Daenerys also burnt a slave-owner alive and
was thrilled to do it.

00:02:22.080 --> 00:02:27.560
She gave a chilling speech about how she deserved
to rule just before she burnt a horde of Dothraki

00:02:27.560 --> 00:02:28.780
warlords to death.

00:02:28.780 --> 00:02:33.840
And who could forget her ruthless flaming
of Samwell Tarly's brother and father, plus

00:02:33.840 --> 00:02:37.680
her execution of Varys that came at the top
of this very episode?

00:02:37.680 --> 00:02:42.380
The season has shown time and time again that
Daenerys isn't afraid of doling out death

00:02:42.380 --> 00:02:46.420
sentences, and she's been pretty clear about
her intentions from the start.

00:02:46.620 --> 00:02:51.840
"We will take back what was stolen from me
and destroy those who have wronged me.

00:02:51.840 --> 00:02:56.460
We will lay waste to armies and burn cities
to the ground."

00:02:56.620 --> 00:03:00.840
But that attitude contrasts harshly to the
other side of her personality, the side that

00:03:00.840 --> 00:03:04.960
frees wrongfully enslaved people, liberates
cities, and promises to "break the wheel"

00:03:04.960 --> 00:03:09.480
of oppression instead of simply taking her
own turn as the person in charge.

00:03:09.480 --> 00:03:13.780
Dany turning into the person she said she
would never become, the woman who strikes

00:03:13.780 --> 00:03:18.770
fear in the hearts of the Westerosi people,
the Queen of the Ashes, the spitting image

00:03:18.770 --> 00:03:23.299
of her father, was shocking to behold even
if there were some breadcrumbs leading up

00:03:23.300 --> 00:03:24.660
to the snapping point.

00:03:24.660 --> 00:03:29.000
Dan Weiss has said he doesn't feel that Daenerys
always intended to burn King's Landing and

00:03:29.000 --> 00:03:33.409
its citizens to a crisp, though there was
a lot of build-up that would show cause for

00:03:33.409 --> 00:03:34.550
her doing so.

00:03:34.550 --> 00:03:38.890
Rather, Weiss noted that Dany decided to take
that course of action the moment she arrived

00:03:38.890 --> 00:03:40.020
in the capital city.

00:03:40.400 --> 00:03:44.860
"It's in that moment on the walls of King's
Landing where she's looking at that symbol

00:03:44.860 --> 00:03:50.420
of everything that was taken from her, when
she makes the decision to make this personal."

00:03:50.600 --> 00:03:55.000
Benioff added that Daenerys may never have
become the Mad Queen if her journey to the

00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:56.840
Iron Throne had played out differently.

00:03:57.080 --> 00:04:00.080
"If circumstances had been different, I don't
think this side of Dany ever would have come

00:04:00.080 --> 00:04:00.700
out.

00:04:00.800 --> 00:04:05.400
If Cersei hadn't betrayed her, if Cersei hadn't
executed Missandei, if Jon hadn't told her

00:04:05.400 --> 00:04:06.400
the truth..."

00:04:06.560 --> 00:04:11.640
Unfortunately, this side of Daenerys Targaryen
did come out, and it will probably be her

00:04:11.640 --> 00:04:12.460
undoing.

00:04:12.620 --> 00:04:17.180
It's tough to imagine the people of Westeros
rallying behind Daenerys after she needlessly

00:04:17.190 --> 00:04:21.440
murdered thousands of people via dragon fire
and decimated the capital.

00:04:21.440 --> 00:04:26.580
Now that she's gone full Mad Queen, Dany likely
can't go back to the person she used to be.

00:04:26.580 --> 00:04:31.560
Her dream to sit on the Iron Throne may never
come true, despite her greatest enemy, Cersei,

00:04:31.560 --> 00:04:36.660
dying in the chaos of the siege and Jon constantly
saying he will always support Dany.

00:04:36.660 --> 00:04:41.080
It will be an intense fight to the finish
during the final episode of Game of Thrones.

00:04:41.080 --> 00:04:44.340
